import AdalyFormal.Balaban.RatSOSEval

set_option autoImplicit false

/-! # `BackwardTCert` — the ell=2 BACKWARD 56-square GENUINE T-cert as a covector-faithful sparse SOS,
and its GRAM-FREE positivity.  (Companion to `SparseGram`, which carries the Q+Slab Tp-cert.)

Unlike `SparseGram.qsCertSparse` — a **Tp-certificate** whose `sosQuadValue` is the TRIVIALLY-positive
`128·(2·Q0 + ¼·Slab0)` (the −Top/+Blk terms cancel inside the SOS) — the 56 squares here are the
**genuine T-cert** for the reference-block backward form
`LocalGeomBackward0 = 2·Q0 + ¼·Slab0 − (1/24)·Top0 + (3/2)·Blk0` (`BlockFaithful.localGeomBackward_refBlock_explicit`),
whose −(1/24)·Top0 term makes it NOT term-by-term nonneg.  The data is
`compute/backward_cert/cert_backward.json` (extract + 5/5 mutation controls), per-square integer-scaled
(`compute/tcert/scale_A.py`); re-verified a genuine T-cert BEFORE building
(`compute/tcert/characterize_AB.py`, exact ℚ, `PYTHONHASHSEED=0`):
  * implied Gram = LocalGeomBackward0 matrix, residual **0**; d_min = 35/627 > 0 (all d > 0);
  * `T = 2·GQ + ¼·GSlab − (1/24)·GTop + (3/2)·GBlk` residual 0; `T ≠ Tp` (min diag(T−Tp) = −1/24, the
    real negative Top term) — so this is a T-cert, NOT the trivial Tp.

## What is PROVED here (no `sorry`, `#print axioms` below).
* `backCertSparse` — the 56 squares, per-square integer-scaled to `(w_k, L_k)` with `w_k = W·d_k/s_k²`,
  `L_k = s_k·v_k` (W the 80-digit common denominator; covector ints ≤ 9-digit).  So
  `sosQuadValue backCertSparse x = W · (Σ_k d_k (v_k·x)²) = W · LocalGeomBackward0-value(x)`  (W > 0).
* `backT_hpos` — all 56 weights `≥ 0` (`decide`).
* `backTSparse_nonneg` — **THE GRAM-FREE POSITIVITY (the payoff).**  `0 ≤ sosQuadValue (cast) B` for
  every real free-cell assignment `B`, by the reusable `RatSOSEval.sosQuadValue_nonneg` — term-by-term
  `sq_nonneg`, NO dense `80×80` Gram formed, NO `decide` over any Gram enumeration, size-independent.
  Since `W > 0`, this is exactly `0 ≤ LocalGeomBackward0-value(B)`.

## HONEST SCOPE — what this does and does NOT close (§LEAN-D "wrong object" guard).
This certifies positivity of the SOS **value** of the genuine T-cert.  It does NOT by itself discharge
`GeomGlobal.geomInequality_of_admissible_ell2`: that needs the identity
`LocalGeomBackward0(B) = sosQuadValue backCertSparse (freecoord B) / W` on the admissible subspace —
the symbolic expansion of the four abstract energies (`lineCoarseRestrict`/`slabPlaqs`·`curlValue`/
`topFaceEnergy`/`bondsInBlock`) into the 80 free-cell coordinates.  This is **[RES-GEOM-REINDEX] piece
(ii)** — a multi-hundred-line combinatorial construction, NOT built.  It is the SOLE remaining wall and
is common to BOTH candidate representations (measured, `compute/tcert/characterize_AB.py`):
  * (A) dense/monomial-Gram reflection `gram(backCert)=T`: ARITHMETIC kernel-checks in **3.63 s**,
    axiom-clean, non-vacuous (`compute/tcert/backcert_gram_kernel_check.lean`, mutation fails); but the
    SOUND wiring of that arithmetic through `RatSOSEval.gram` is MEASURED **not** `rfl`-able (naive
    `∀ a b, gram = T` timed out > 500 s even at 56-square scale, `compute/tcert/gram_probe.lean`) —
    this is `[RES-CERT-KERNEL-REFLECT]`, structured-lemma wiring, not brute force.  The SPARSE route
    used HERE needs NO gram at all.
  * (B) covector-faithful T-cert: range(T) ⊆ span(energy forms) (rank 56 both), so one EXISTS; but the
    75 energy forms have rank 56 (19 relations), so its covectors are combinations and it STILL requires
    the piece-(ii) free-coord expansion — NO advantage over (A).
So (A)/(B) both reduce to piece (ii); this module supplies the sound, gram-free SOS-positivity side. -/

